# 🌾 Seasonal Agriculture Performance Analysis

An end-to-end data analytics project investigating seasonal variations in agricultural performance, crop yield productivity, water efficiency, and farm profitability using Python. Developed for the **VOIS AICTE Industry Internship Program**.

---

## 📌 Project Overview

Agricultural activities are heavily influenced by seasonal variations in environmental conditions, farming practices, and market prices. This project analyzes 4,000 agricultural farm records spanning three primary Indian cropping seasons—**Kharif**, **Rabi**, and **Zaid**[cite: 1]. 

By cleaning, feature-engineering, and analyzing raw operational metrics, this project identifies critical performance bottlenecks and offers evidence-based recommendations for seasonal farm planning[cite: 1].

---

## 🎯 End Users & Stakeholders

* **Farmers & Farm Managers:** Optimizing seasonal crop selection and switching to precision irrigation systems[cite: 1].
* **Agricultural Policy Makers:** Planning regional water allocation, subsidies, and price protection for food staples[cite: 1].
* **Agri-Tech & Input Suppliers:** Forecasting demand for seeds, fertilizers, and pest management products by season[cite: 1].
* **Data Analysts & Researchers:** Evaluating climate impacts and building predictive yield models[cite: 1].

---

## 📊 Key Analytical Findings

| Performance Metric | Kharif Season | Rabi Season | Zaid Season | Core Insight |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Sample Count** | 1,779 | 1,627 | 594 | Cultivation heavily favors Kharif and Rabi cycles[cite: 1]. |
| **Avg. Yield (t/ha)** | **5.63** | 5.09 | 4.64 | Kharif leads productivity by ~10.6% over Rabi[cite: 1]. |
| **Avg. Profit (INR)** | **₹1,78,914.65** | ₹87,689.47 | **-₹24,804.82** | Zaid operates at an average loss due to high input overhead[cite: 1]. |
| **Avg. Rainfall (mm)** | **852.11** | 435.94 | 299.12 | Kharif benefits directly from monsoon precipitation[cite: 1]. |
| **Disease / Pest Risk** | **54.47%** | 40.48% | 38.22% | Elevated humidity in Kharif increases pest vulnerability[cite: 1]. |
| **Water Efficiency** | **5.89** | 5.19 | 4.41 | Efficiency declines in dry seasons due to heavy reliance on irrigation[cite: 1]. |

---

## 💡 Key Takeaways & Recommendations

1. **Precision Irrigation in Zaid:** Shift off-season cultivation from flood irrigation to drip systems to increase water efficiency and reduce losses[cite: 1].
2. **Preventive Pest Control in Kharif:** Implement early pest mitigation prior to the monsoon season to minimize humidity-driven crop damage[cite: 1].
3. **Crop-Season Realignment:** Encourage high-value cash crops (**Sugarcane**, **Chilli**) while optimizing subsidies for staple food grains (**Wheat**, **Rice**) facing narrow profit margins[cite: 1].

---

## 🛠️ Technology Stack

* **Language:** Python 3.x[cite: 1]
* **Data Manipulation:** Pandas, NumPy[cite: 1]
* **Visualization:** Matplotlib, Seaborn[cite: 1]
* **Environment:** Jupyter Notebook / VS Code[cite: 1]
* **Data File:** Microsoft Excel (`.xlsx`)[cite: 1]

